r goal is to examine the impact of anti-­corruption campaign on SOEs' OFDI. A difference-­\nin-­difference (DID) model is applied for this study. Following Card (1990), Card and Krueger \n(1994), and Duflo (2001), the empirical model designed for firm-­country-­year data structure has \nthe following form:\n(1)\nYijt = 훼+ 훽DIDSOEi × Anti2013 + 훽ControlControlsjt + 휇i + 휂j + 휆t + 휀ijt\nYijt indicates the number of OFDI projects firm i has invested or the amount of its investment \nvalue in country j in year t. SOEi indicate firm i's ownership, it equals one when firm i is SOE, \nand it equals zero when firm i is POE. The Chinese government administration began a massive \nanti-­corruption campaign in 2013 which continues to the present. A dummy variable is used to \nindicate the period before and after 2013. When year ≥2013, Anti2013 = 1, which represents that \nthe anti-­corruption campaign has had an impact. When the year <2013, Anti2013 = 0, this indi-\ncates that that year was not affected by the anti-­corruption campaign.\n 14679701, 2022, 9, Downloaded from https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/twec.13244 by University Of Sydney, Wiley Online Library on [27/10/2024]. See the Terms and Conditions (https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/terms-and-conditions) on Wiley Online Library for rules of use; OA articles are governed by the applicable Creative Commons License--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nevident: Evidence Factors in Observational Studies (https://erised.las.iastate.edu/CRAN/web/packages/evident/evident.pdf)\nciteturn10search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; These data are used to illustrate matching to form matched triples from three groups, Pennsylvania ... optmach package, accept its academic license, and install the approxmatch package. ... Using a different matched sample, an analysis of two evidence factors in Card and Krueger’s study ... B. (1994) <doi:10.1080/10618600.2019.1584900> \"Min